WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.502 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:05.805
-At the end of last week's
"Corrections,"

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.476
I asked Shoemaker,
"Is it pencil?"

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.511
before I attempted to bite
into the pencil

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.848
to prove whether or not it was
a real pencil or a candy pencil.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.617
A lot of you thought
this was in reference

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:20.452
to the television show
"Is It Cake?"

00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:23.455
hosted by our friend Mikey Day.

00:00:23.455 --> 00:00:25.791
And I was surprised
that all of you referenced

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:29.328
that show, not knowing
that is not the original.

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:33.833
The original host
of "Is It Cake?" was...

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.704
First of all,
it aired in the '70s on BBC

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.405
and it was hosted
not by Mikey Day

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:44.677
but by British legend
of stage and screen

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:45.678
Alex--

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:49.148
Excuse me.
Sir Laurence Olivier.

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:51.717
We did some digging
and we found a clip

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:54.387
of the popular original version
of "Is It Cake?"

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.889
Let's take a look.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.057
-Take your time.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.726
Tell me.

00:01:00.726 --> 00:01:02.128
Is it [dubbed voice] cake?

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.164
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.603
-These jokes, correction jokes
aren't sprints.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.472
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.544
In "Roadhouse,"
Patrick Swayze

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:21.080
wasn't a bouncer,
he was a cooler.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.716
This was something his character
made clear many times.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.285
The problem is --
I knew that.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:28.754
The problem is,
William H. Macy was in a movie,

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:31.624
a different movie in 2003,
called "The Cooler,"

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:34.627
and he's my cooler.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.295
Sorry to say it.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:37.730
In the order...

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:42.535
I love Swayze, but in
the pecking order of actors,

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.603
it is always been, for me --

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:46.472
doesn't have to be
the same for everybody --

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.942
Macy, Swayze, Kevin Spacey.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:53.379
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:56.315
Oh, I also love Jake Lacy.

00:01:56.315 --> 00:01:58.784
So now top three
could be anywhere,

00:01:58.784 --> 00:02:01.988
but it's like Lacy, Macy,
Swayze, Kevin Spacey,

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.489
and then...

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.658
John Wayne Gacy.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:09.462
The -- For the serial killing.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.465
Not the painting.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.633
Long story.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:20.239
Shoemaker is a huge fan of
John Wayne Gacy, the painter.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:25.378
And so he's very upset
anytime you lump the two.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.012
And he's always walking
around saying,

00:02:27.012 --> 00:02:29.581
"I'm sorry that I can separate
the art from the artist!"

00:02:29.581 --> 00:02:31.250
And I'm like, "What?"

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.086
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.391
A lot of you will sometimes
reference and write

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.393
about Shoemaker
in the comments section,

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:44.563
and a lot of you guess at
the spelling of his name.

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:47.566
It's not your fault, you know.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:50.069
Well, actually,
there are credits on the show.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.172
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.209
Like I'd say,
maybe you don't have time

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.545
to watch the credits, but, uh...

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:03.216
you're leaving comments
in the YouTube section.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.550
Anyways, in case
you want to know,

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.719
that is how you spell it.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.555
We also accept that emoji.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.558
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.060
Um...

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.164
Oh, we did a joke
about "Family Feud"

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:22.435
and we were told we used
an incorrect buzzer sound

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.670
for "Family Feud,"
which shocked me.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.674
I could not -- I went back.
I could not hear the difference.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:29.475
First, let's hear
the real sound effect.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.477
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.946
And now let's hear the one
we used in "A Closer Look."

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:35.348
Then every time they do

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.183
another failed roll call,
it can end like this.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:39.518
-A speaker has not been elected.

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:41.120
-[Deep voice] Buzzzzz!

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.156
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.331
-Somebody wrote in,
"A GoPro camera is bigger

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:53.499
than a squirrel's head."

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.301
Maybe where you live,
but not in New York.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.969
We got some...

00:03:56.969 --> 00:04:00.172
jacked squirrels.

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:02.008
Not your, like, Monday
through Friday squirrels.

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:04.744
But in the park
on the weekends

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.913
when the bridge-and-tunnel
squirrels come in,

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:09.582
just walking...

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.517
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:15.254
[ New Jersey accent ] "I got
your nuts right over here!"

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.290
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:25.632
Kevin McCarthy boldly proclaimed
he could count.

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:28.133
We said that wasn't
that impressive

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:32.138
'cause it's a Sesame Street
character skill.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:34.306
We had him say, "I can count,"

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:35.841
showed a picture of The Count.

00:04:35.841 --> 00:04:37.075
"I have a sweet tooth,"

00:04:37.075 --> 00:04:39.078
showed a picture
of Cookie Monster.

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.847
"Me very ticklish,"
showed a picture of Elmo.

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.915
Got it wrong

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:45.150
because Elmo only says "Elmo."

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.352
Cookie Monster says "me."

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.686
It should have been,
"I can count,

00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:49.154
me have sweet tooth,

00:04:49.154 --> 00:04:50.656
Kevin very ticklish."

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:53.025
Thank you.
A lot of you wrote that in.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:54.527
We also said Kevin McCarthy is

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:55.862
second in line
to the presidency,

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:58.865
and a lot of you said
he's third in line.

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:01.067
The thing is, I don't think

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.902
President Biden is in line.

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:06.238
You know,
I think he has the job.

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:08.374
Kamala is first in line.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.175
Kevin McCarthy
is second in line.

00:05:10.175 --> 00:05:11.744
So, that's maybe
just a difference.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.479
I see where we've split there,

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.814
but I do hold fast
to the way we went.

00:05:15.814 --> 00:05:16.983
Also, this is interesting.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.485
We do have a succession plan

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.787
here at "Late Night," as well.

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:23.789
After me, it's Amber.

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:26.792
And after Amber, it's Scollins.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:30.262
So if anything happens to me,
Amber takes over.

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:32.098
And if anything happens
to Amber,

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:34.267
arrest Scollins!

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.336
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:40.340
[ Clears throat ]

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:45.978
I was doing my
Jennifer Coolidge impression.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:48.948
To great acclaim,
it should be noted.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:52.484
And I was a little taken aback
by this comment.

00:05:52.484 --> 00:05:53.986
"Who's Tanya?

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:55.621
This might not be
an obscure reference,

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:56.822
and if I look it up

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:58.323
and it's simply some
'White Lotus' reference,

00:05:58.323 --> 00:05:59.926
then you're writing staff
should be ashamed.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:02.661
Not all of your audience
is watching 'White Lotus'

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:03.829
or 'Real Housewives'

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:05.564
or whatever show
that reference was from.

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:07.466
If you do not include
the subject of the reference,

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:09.702
you might as well be writing
inside jokes for 'Corrections.'"

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.136
And at that,
all I have to say is,

00:06:11.136 --> 00:06:12.805
[as Coolidge] Wowwwww.

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.874
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:24.149
[Normal voice] The jackal mugs
obviously have been going out.

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:26.986
People are very happy.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:30.990
Someone thought this was
a nice thing to write.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.058
"I feel like it's important for
everyone to know that sometimes,

00:06:33.058 --> 00:06:35.628
occasionally someone breaks
into my apartment building,

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.797
opens up everyone's packages
and takes what they want.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:40.298
My jackal mug had arrived
while I was out of town,

00:06:40.298 --> 00:06:42.368
and I received a notification
about another robbery.

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:44.570
I was so sad,
but there was a twist.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:48.908
The thief opened the box and
then declined to take the mug."

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:51.110
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:58.784
We did a bit about
Benjamin Franklin

00:06:58.784 --> 00:07:00.052
trash-talking Thomas Jefferson

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.655
during the
Constitutional Convention,

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:06.225
and many of you correctly
pointed out Thomas Jefferson

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:08.293
was not at the Constitutional
Convention because

00:07:08.293 --> 00:07:11.897
he was serving as ambassador
to France at the time.

00:07:11.897 --> 00:07:13.399
Very embarrassed.

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:16.235
Very embarrassed anytime we make
a historical error.

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.904
We try to be accurate
about history

00:07:18.904 --> 00:07:20.907
as much as possible
in the body of the show.

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:22.275
It's an unforgivable error,

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:24.777
especially we think about
all the history scholars

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:26.378
who have provided
their scholarship to us.

00:07:26.378 --> 00:07:27.547
It would be easy enough

00:07:27.547 --> 00:07:29.215
anytime we talk about history
to Google it

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:30.583
and make sure
we get it right.

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:33.252
It was very flippant of us.

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:35.588
It's beneath us.

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:37.022
Clearly, what
I should have said

00:07:37.022 --> 00:07:39.224
is Benjamin Franklin
trash-talked Thomas Jefferson

00:07:39.224 --> 00:07:42.228
during the Constitution
Convention during a phone call.

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:44.363
[ Laughter ]

00:07:46.765 --> 00:07:49.034
We talked about how the Steelers
were eliminated

00:07:49.034 --> 00:07:51.870
from the playoffs
after the Jets failed to win.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:56.041
And we showed a picture of Jets
quarterback Mike White.

00:07:56.041 --> 00:07:59.478
And someone pointed out
Mike White didn't actually play

00:07:59.478 --> 00:08:01.280
in the Jets game on Sunday.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.915
And all I want
to say to that is,

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:05.418
maybe he [bleep] should have.

00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:08.220
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:09.588
[ Sarcastically ]
Oh, no, we got to figure out

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:11.924
what we got here
with Joe Flacco.

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:13.960
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:20.232
I said all dads watch
"Yellowstone."

00:08:20.232 --> 00:08:22.435
Someone wrote in and said,
"I'm a father of two

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:23.768
and I've never seen
that show."

00:08:23.768 --> 00:08:25.271
Well, bad news, bro --

00:08:25.271 --> 00:08:26.939
Those aren't your kids.

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:29.008
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.813 --> 00:08:37.649
We talked about the way

00:08:37.649 --> 00:08:39.685
Mike Pence claps.

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:44.122
And first of all,
we said that he should be

00:08:44.122 --> 00:08:46.458
holding two coconuts
like he was in

00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:47.793
"Monty Python
and the Holy Grail."

00:08:47.793 --> 00:08:49.628
Two halves of coconuts.

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:51.129
That was an error.

00:08:51.129 --> 00:08:53.298
But, um...

00:08:53.298 --> 00:08:56.301
Someone pointed out a really
shocking thing to me.

00:08:56.301 --> 00:08:59.638
'Cause I then mimed Mike Pence
running and clapping,

00:08:59.638 --> 00:09:01.607
and they said,
"You're clapping wrong.

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:03.476
Mike Pence claps like this."

00:09:05.911 --> 00:09:08.247
And I said that couldn't
possibly be right.

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:09.915
And then I went back
and took a look.

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:11.284
Let's see.

00:09:17.155 --> 00:09:18.991
What the [bleep] is that?

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:19.992
[ Laughter ]

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:22.028
Look at that again up close.

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:31.937
That was like one of the tests
they did in "Blade Runner."

00:09:31.937 --> 00:09:33.673
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:36.174
They were like, "Clap."

00:09:36.174 --> 00:09:38.577
If you did this,
that's how they knew.

00:09:38.577 --> 00:09:41.247
[ Laughter ]

00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:43.749
Oh, we had a headline
about some high schoolers,

00:09:43.749 --> 00:09:45.418
a New York Post fake headline.

00:09:45.418 --> 00:09:47.819
And one of the high schoolers
was named Keith.

00:09:47.819 --> 00:09:50.389
And someone wrote in and said
there are no Gen Z people

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:52.892
named Keith.

00:09:52.892 --> 00:09:55.728
So if you're Gen Z
and your name is Keith,

00:09:55.728 --> 00:09:59.365 line:0%
please go -- please go
to @seacaptainpolls,

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:01.433 line:0%
where we're gonna post the poll,

00:10:01.433 --> 00:10:04.170 line:0%
"Are you Gen Z?
And if so, is your name Keith?"

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.172
[ Laughter ]

00:10:07.506 --> 00:10:09.174
We talk about our crew
a lot here.

00:10:09.174 --> 00:10:11.943
And obviously we had --
our edible pencils were out

00:10:11.943 --> 00:10:14.446
and we've been talking about --

00:10:14.446 --> 00:10:16.081
the kindness of
the edible pencils

00:10:16.081 --> 00:10:20.986
came from the mother of our
sound mixer, Mike Witzer.

00:10:20.986 --> 00:10:22.421
And a bunch of you said,

00:10:22.421 --> 00:10:24.590
"Are you really saying
you have a sound mixer

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:26.225
named Mike Witzer?"

00:10:26.225 --> 00:10:28.060
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.228
And I never put it tog--

00:10:29.228 --> 00:10:33.065
It does sound like
a children's book.

00:10:33.065 --> 00:10:34.633
"Iggy Peck, Architect."

00:10:34.633 --> 00:10:36.035
"Rosie Revere, Engineer."

00:10:36.035 --> 00:10:38.104
"Mike Witzer, Sound Mixer."

00:10:38.104 --> 00:10:40.773
[ Laughter ]

00:10:40.773 --> 00:10:42.941
But of course, we know it's not
a family business, right?

00:10:42.941 --> 00:10:44.610
Like, his mom's
not a sound mixer.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:47.012
She's a candy maker.

00:10:47.012 --> 00:10:50.082
Of course,
Witzer isn't her maiden name.

00:10:50.082 --> 00:10:52.751
I asked Mike what her name
was before she was married.

00:10:52.751 --> 00:10:54.420
Mandy Baker.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.555
[ Laughter ]

00:11:00.893 --> 00:11:04.429
Ooh, sometimes jackals
really do impress me.

00:11:04.429 --> 00:11:06.065
And I'm willing --
I'm always willing to share

00:11:06.065 --> 00:11:08.901
when I'm impressed
by a jackal comment.

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:11.770
We told an Amelia Earhart
joke yesterday.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:14.974
Did not go great
with the audience.

00:11:16.508 --> 00:11:18.577
Someone wrote,
"You can't be surprised

00:11:18.577 --> 00:11:21.413
when an Amelia Earhart joke
doesn't land."

00:11:21.413 --> 00:11:23.249
[ Laughter ]

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:37.396
Someone sent a package
to our P.O. box,

00:11:37.396 --> 00:11:40.433
and it was addressed to Wally.

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:46.271
I opened it --
out of kindness.

00:11:46.271 --> 00:11:48.641
Because, you know, it was
to Wally, so I assumed

00:11:48.641 --> 00:11:50.275
it would be, like,

00:11:50.275 --> 00:11:52.011
dog [bleep] or anthrax.

00:11:52.011 --> 00:11:54.113
[ Laughter ]

00:11:57.616 --> 00:11:59.418
But I forgot, Wally is beloved.

00:11:59.418 --> 00:12:02.087
And this is -- it was tiny.

00:12:02.087 --> 00:12:03.555
It was in a package, right?

00:12:03.555 --> 00:12:05.323
I'm seeing this,
and it was in a bigger package.

00:12:05.323 --> 00:12:07.126
I'm like, "Oh, this is gonna be
some bull[bleep] joke," right?

00:12:07.126 --> 00:12:10.462
So I unwrapped it.

00:12:10.462 --> 00:12:11.831
And, uh...

00:12:13.865 --> 00:12:16.167
This is incredible.

00:12:16.167 --> 00:12:17.536
Look at that little...

00:12:17.536 --> 00:12:18.603
Can you get in close enough?

00:12:18.603 --> 00:12:20.105
"Jackals rule."

00:12:20.105 --> 00:12:24.275
And a very --
a very believable Wally.

00:12:24.275 --> 00:12:28.446
This is art, Shoemaker --

00:12:28.446 --> 00:12:30.449
not your clown paintings.

00:12:30.449 --> 00:12:33.018
[ Laughter ]

00:12:33.018 --> 00:12:35.488
Anyway, that's our --
that's our tiny Wally,

00:12:35.488 --> 00:12:37.689
and I'm gonna give it to him

00:12:37.689 --> 00:12:39.958
as soon as he can prove

00:12:39.958 --> 00:12:42.795
it's legally his
if it goes to my P.O. box.

00:12:42.795 --> 00:12:44.830
[ Laughter ]

00:12:47.132 --> 00:12:48.634
Shoemaker is real, by the way.

00:12:48.634 --> 00:12:50.302
Some of you been positing that

00:12:50.302 --> 00:12:54.640
he's like a Tyler Durden
from "Fight Club" situation.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.041
[ Laughter ]

00:12:56.041 --> 00:12:59.711
Like he's a figment
of my imagination.

00:12:59.711 --> 00:13:02.748
Let me tell you how I know it's
not a Tyler Durden situation.

00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:05.250
Shoemaker has never walked
into a room and had someone say,

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:06.985
"Whoa, is that Brad Pitt?"

00:13:06.985 --> 00:13:08.153
Only...

00:13:08.153 --> 00:13:10.322
[ Laughter ]

00:13:10.322 --> 00:13:11.656
Different faces.

00:13:11.656 --> 00:13:14.993
Exact same body, I should note.

00:13:14.993 --> 00:13:16.829
Shoemaker's super jacked.

00:13:16.829 --> 00:13:19.931
Thin jacked.

00:13:19.931 --> 00:13:22.701
And the amount he has
his shirt off in the office!

00:13:22.701 --> 00:13:23.835
[ Laughter ]

00:13:23.835 --> 00:13:26.839
Always something.

00:13:26.839 --> 00:13:30.008
Loves it.
Loves to flaunt it.

00:13:30.008 --> 00:13:32.877
Like, I'll hear like hammering
through our shared wall

00:13:32.877 --> 00:13:36.682
and I'll go in and he's, like,
on a chair, shirt off.

00:13:36.682 --> 00:13:39.418
Got, like, nails in his mouth
and he's like,

00:13:39.418 --> 00:13:41.420
"Got to get the new Gacy up."

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.522
[ Laughter ]

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:51.463
We made a joke about...

00:13:51.463 --> 00:13:54.099
the scariest thing
someone could send me

00:13:54.099 --> 00:13:56.768
is a severed human head.

00:13:56.768 --> 00:13:59.238
Turns out I was wrong.

00:13:59.238 --> 00:14:00.939
Opened this right before
the show today.

00:14:00.939 --> 00:14:03.942
This is not the first time
I'm saying this.

00:14:03.942 --> 00:14:07.445
I was right on some accounts
when I said a severed human head

00:14:07.445 --> 00:14:09.548
would be the scariest thing
you could receive.

00:14:09.548 --> 00:14:11.550
My mistake was the word "human,"

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.552
because this came.

00:14:13.552 --> 00:14:15.454
[ Laughter ]

00:14:18.323 --> 00:14:20.225
And I'm not saying
you owe me an apology,

00:14:20.225 --> 00:14:24.362
but you should
apologize to Donna,

00:14:24.362 --> 00:14:27.700
who had to run to wardrobe

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.567
and get a new pair of pants

00:14:29.567 --> 00:14:31.904
after I [bleep]
the ones I was wearing.

00:14:31.904 --> 00:14:33.906
[ Laughter ]

00:14:36.608 --> 00:14:39.110
Well, you guys...

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:41.113
[ Laughs ]

00:14:41.113 --> 00:14:43.115
[ Laughter ]

00:14:49.188 --> 00:14:50.890
Is it Wally?

00:14:52.925 --> 00:14:53.959
Is it W--
[ Laughs ]

00:14:53.959 --> 00:14:55.928
Not doing this. Bye!
See me next week.

